# Docs And URLs

-   Use `https://v4.zelf.world` for Tags, other v3.6 surfaces, and Zelf ID (`/api/zelf-ids`) documentation examples.
-   Use localhost URLs only for local testing, and prefer an explicit `PORT` over relying on repository fallbacks.
-   Public API docs belong in `zelf-documentation/docs/api/`.
-   Include the auth flow when documenting protected endpoints: session creation, JWT extraction, then authenticated API calls.
-   Document both success and error responses with real status codes and validation behavior.
-   Prefer Docusaurus tabs when documenting multiple example languages.
-   Keep language coverage aligned with the current backend standard: cURL, Node.js, Python, PHP, and Rust when the endpoint warrants full docs.

